{"abstract":"Objectives Earlier studies on the association between plasma lipid profiles and functional somatic disorders (FSD) are mainly small case control studies hampered by selection bias and do not consider the great overlap between the various FSDs. The aim of the present study was to investigate the associations between various FSDs and plasma lipid profiles (total cholesterol, HDL cholesterol, non-HDL cholesterol and triglycerides) in a large, unselected population. Design A cross-sectional general population-based study Setting The Danish Study of Functional Somatic Disorders (DanFunD) conducted in 2011–2015 in 10 municipalities in the western part of greater Copenhagen, Denmark. Participants A total of 8,608 men and women aged 18–76 years were included in the analyses. Various delimitations of FSD such as chronic fatigue, chronic widespread pain, irritable bowel, and bodily distress syndrome were measured using validated self-administrated questionnaires. Lipid parameters were measured from fasting plasma samples using colorimetric slide methods with Vitros 4600/5600 Ortho Clinical Diagnostics. Outcome measures Logistic regression analyses were used to calculate possible associations between plasma lipids and the various delimitations of FSD. Associations are presented by OR (95% CI) and shown in boxplots. Results We found a positive association between bodily distress syndrome and triglycerides and non-HDL cholesterol and a negative association with HDL-cholesterol, but no consistent association with total cholesterol. A similar pattern was observed for persons with chronic fatigue, and to some degree for persons with chronic widespread pain, whereas persons with irritable bowel did not show a clear association with the lipid profiles. Conclusion This is the first major study on plasma lipid profiles and FSD indicating an association between some delimitations of FSD and an unfavorable lipid profile. Due to the cross-sectional design, it cannot be determined whether the findings are consequences or determinants of FSD. Further studies–preferable prospective studies—are needed.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Torben","Jacobsen, Rikke","Sæbye, Ditte","Petersen, Marie Weinreich","Fink, Per","Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","Linneberg, Allan","Bjerregaard, Anne Ahrendt","Schovsbo, Signe Ulfbeck","Benros, Michael Eriksen","Eplov, Lene Falgaard","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz"],"cuid":["S02-088.00-716015"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Torben"],"keyword":["Cholesterol","Cholesterol HDL","Chronic pain","Cross Sectional Studies","Fatigue","Fatigue Syndrome Chronic epidemiology","Female","Humans","Irritable bowel syndrome","Lipid Metabolism","Male","Prospective Studies","Triglycerides"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lipid metabolism and functional somatic disorders in the general population the danfund study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0296799","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.00-716015","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10817187","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85183486050","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38277392","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-7bbd6e51-32be-4c84-9879-509e1538cc0a","ku-07bc3c0c-8037-435c-a3e5-6fc73f867027"],"keyword":["Cholesterol","Cholesterol, HDL","Chronic Pain","Cross-Sectional Studies","Fatigue","Fatigue Syndrome, Chronic/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Irritable Bowel Syndrome","Lipid Metabolism","Male","Prospective Studies","Triglycerides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9B2C67C4A007ED6B191697297DCD6F47"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/382440773/journal.pone.0296799_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0296799","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Research clinic for gambling addiction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Torben","key":"jørgensentorbenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Torben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rikke Kart","key":"jacobsenrikkekartpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Rikke Kart","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte","key":"sæbyedittepau","last":"Sæbye","name":"Sæbye, Ditte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Weinreich","key":"petersenmarieweinreichpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9dacce30-6a88-4fa2-a71a-87cccaf540af","name":"Petersen, Marie Weinreich","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"finkperpau","last":"Fink","locid":"22d646ca-5dee-456c-ae39-6c0687a18ce8","name":"Fink, Per","orcid":"0000-0003-2921-4099","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise","key":"gormsenlisekirstinepau","last":"Gormsen","locid":"5516e253-cc95-468b-b53d-b6d1758f9884","name":"Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","name_org":"Gormsen, Lise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergallanpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Ahrendt","key":"bjerregaardanneahrendtpau","last":"Bjerregaard","name":"Bjerregaard, Anne Ahrendt","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Signe Ulfbeck","key":"schovsbosigneulfbeckpau","last":"Schovsbo","name":"Schovsbo, Signe Ulfbeck","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Eriksen","key":"benrosmichaeleriksenpau","last":"Benros","name":"Benros, Michael Eriksen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Falgaard","key":"eplovlenefalgaardpau","last":"Eplov","name":"Eplov, Lene Falgaard","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenniklasryepau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas Meinertz","key":"dantoftthomasmeinertzpau","last":"Dantoft","name":"Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38277392"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0296799","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"1","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0296799","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183486050"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7bbd6e51-32be-4c84-9879-509e1538cc0a","ku-07bc3c0c-8037-435c-a3e5-6fc73f867027"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lipid metabolism and functional somatic disorders in the general population. The DanFunD study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.00-716015","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Flucloxacillin is a widely used antibiotic. It is an agonist to the nuclear receptor PXR that regulates the expression of cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzymes. Treatment with flucloxacillin reduces warfarin efficacy and plasma concentrations of tacrolimus, voriconazole, and repaglinide. We conducted a translational study to investigate if flucloxacillin induces CYP enzymes. We also investigated if flucloxacillin induces its own metabolism as an autoinducer. We performed a randomized, unblinded, two-period, cross-over, clinical pharmacokinetic cocktail study. Twelve healthy adults completed the study. They ingested 1 g flucloxacillin 3 times daily for 31 days, and we assessed the full pharmacokinetics of the Basel cocktail drugs on days 0, 10, and 28, and plasma concentrations of flucloxacillin on days 0, 9, and 27. The 3D spheroid of primary human hepatocytes (PHHs) were exposed to flucloxacillin (concentration range: 0.15–250 μM) for 96 hours. Induction of mRNA expression, protein abundance, and enzyme activity of CYP enzymes were assessed. Flucloxacillin treatment reduced the metabolic ratio of midazolam (CYP3A4), (geometric mean ratio (GMR) 10 days (95% confidence interval (CI)): 0.75 (0.64–0.89)) and (GMR 28 days (95% CI): 0.72 (0.62–0.85)). Plasma concentrations of flucloxacillin did not change during 27 days of treatment. Flucloxacillin caused concentration-dependent induction of CYP3A4 and CYP2B6 (mRNA, protein, and activity), CYP2C9 (mRNA and protein), CYP2C19 (mRNA and activity), and CYP2D6 (activity) in 3D spheroid PHH. In conclusion, flucloxacillin is a weak inducer of CYP3A4, which may lead to clinically relevant drug–drug interactions for some narrow therapeutic range drugs that are substrates of CYP3A4.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Iversen, Ditte Bork","Dunvald, Ann-Cathrine","Jespersen, Daniel M","Nielsen, Flemming","Brøsen, Kim","Damkier, Per","Hammer, Helen S","Pötz, Oliver","Järvinen, Erkka","Stage, Tore Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-714320"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stage, Tore Bjerregaard"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Signatope GmbH","University of Tuebingen, Tuebingen, Germany"],"keyword":["Adult","Cytochrome P 450 CYP3A genetics","Cytochrome P 450 Enzyme System metabolism","Drug Interactions","Floxacillin pharmacology","Hepatocytes metabolism","Humans","RNA Messenger"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Otterup Pharmacy"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flucloxacillin is a weak inducer of cyp000000000003a000000000004 in healthy adults and 000000000003d spheroid of primary human hepatocytes","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cpt.2959","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-714320","identifier":[{"id":"37235733","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85161430900","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-8aeb09bc-82ad-4863-bf5f-9b104a292877"],"keyword":["Adult","Cytochrome P-450 CYP3A/genetics","Cytochrome P-450 Enzyme System/metabolism","Drug Interactions","Floxacillin/pharmacology","Hepatocytes/metabolism","Humans","RNA, Messenger"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E0387CA58ED0B5A063832232CD013E7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/cpt.2959","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/252285395/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","