{"abstract":"Safe and effective use of drugs requires an understanding of metabolism and transport. We identified the 100 most prescribed drugs in six countries and conducted a literature search on in vitro data to assess contribution of Phase I and II enzymes and drug transporters to metabolism and transport. Eighty-nine of the 100 drugs undergo drug metabolism or are known substrates for drug transporters. Phase I enzymes are involved in metabolism of 67 drugs, while Phase II enzymes mediate metabolism of 18 drugs. CYP3A4/5 is the most important Phase I enzyme involved in metabolism of 43 drugs followed by CYP2D6 (23 drugs), CYP2C9 (23 drugs), CYP2C19 (22 drugs), CYP1A2 (14 drugs) and CYP2C8 (11 drugs). More than half of the drugs (54 drugs) are known substrates for drug transporters. P-glycoprotein (P-gp) is known to be involved in transport of 30 drugs, while breast cancer resistance protein (BCRP) facilitates transport of 11 drugs. A considerable proportion of drugs are subject to a combination of Phase I metabolism, Phase II metabolism and/or drug transport. We conclude that the majority of the most frequently prescribed drugs depend on drug metabolism or drug transport. Thus, understanding variability of drug metabolism and transport remains a priority.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Iversen, Ditte Bork","Andersen, Nanna Elman","Dunvald, Ann-Cathrine","Pottegård, Anton","Stage, Tore Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-576212"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Stage, Tore Bjerregaard"],"keyword":["ADME","ATP Binding Cassette Transporter Subfamily B Member 1 metabolism","CYP3A4","Cytochrome P 450 CYP1A2 metabolism","Cytochrome P 450 CYP2C19 metabolism","Cytochrome P 450 CYP2C8 metabolism","Cytochrome P 450 CYP2C9 metabolism","Cytochrome P 450 CYP2D6 metabolism","Cytochrome P 450 CYP3A metabolism","Cytochrome P 450 Enzyme System metabolism","Drug metabolism","Drug transport","Membrane Transport Proteins metabolism","Microsomes Liver","Neoplasm Proteins metabolism","P gp"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug metabolism and drug transport of the 000000000100 most prescribed oral drugs","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13780","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-576212","identifier":[{"id":"35972991","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9804310","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85136778431","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-0a99b91e-219a-4880-a119-159162a84f34"],"keyword":["ADME","ATP Binding Cassette Transporter, Subfamily B, Member 1/metabolism","ATP Binding Cassette Transporter, Subfamily G, Member 2","CYP3A4","Cytochrome P-450 CYP1A2/metabolism","Cytochrome P-450 CYP2C19/metabolism","Cytochrome P-450 CYP2C8/metabolism","Cytochrome P-450 CYP2C9/metabolism","Cytochrome P-450 CYP2D6/metabolism","Cytochrome P-450 CYP3A/metabolism","Cytochrome P-450 Enzyme System/metabolism","Membrane Transport Proteins/metabolism","Microsomes, Liver","Neoplasm Proteins/metabolism","P-gp","drug metabolism","drug transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33A227E9046B80EC2B498C8E5474D225"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13780","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/208973272/Basic_Clin_Pharma_Tox_2022_Iversen_Drug_metabolism_and_drug_transport_of_the_100_most_prescribed_oral_drugs.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology, Pharmacy and Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte B","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"7e67054c-25a8-4498-ba58-0b377014cfb8","name":"Iversen, Ditte Bork","name_org":"Iversen, Ditte B","orcid":"0000-0002-5519-9091","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Elman","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"00f385a0-a339-4dfd-87a4-c1ea54bac2bc","name":"Andersen, Nanna Elman","orcid":"0000-0001-5750-8911","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Cathrine","key":"dalgårddunvaldpau","last":"Dalgård Dunvald","locid":"0cc5ad63-2aa5-48e4-94cb-655a8b0a5394","name":"Dunvald, Ann-Cathrine","name_org":"Dalgård Dunvald, Ann-Cathrine","orcid":"0000-0001-7574-0909","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tore B","key":"stagepau","last":"Stage","locid":"b794c141-d9c5-4082-b8c5-b69f854d4c7c","name":"Stage, Tore Bjerregaard","name_org":"Stage, Tore B","orcid":"0000-0002-4698-4389","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35972991"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.13780","issn":["17427835"],"issue":"5","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"311-324","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","volume":"131"},"review"