{"abstract":"The 'thrifty phenotype' hypothesis proposed that fetal undernutrition increases risk of diabetes in later life. Undernourished low birthweight Indian babies are paradoxically more adipose compared to well-nourished European babies, and are at higher risk of diabetes in later life. Twin pregnancies are an example of in utero growth restrictive environment due to shared maternal nutrition. There are few studies of body composition in twins. We performed secondary analysis of anthropometric body composition of twins and singletons in Guinea-Bissau, an economically deprived African country. Anthropometric data were available on 7-34 year-old twins (n = 209, 97 males) and singletons (n = 182, 86 males) in the Guinea-Bissau Twin Registry at the Bandim Health Project. Twins had lower birthweight (2420 vs 3100 g, p < 0.001); and at follow-up, lower height (HAZ mean Z-score difference, -0.21, p = 0.055), weight (WAZ -0.73, p = 0.024) and BMI (BAZ -0.22, p = 0.079) compared to singletons but higher adiposity (skinfolds: +0.33 SD, p = 0.001). Twins also had higher fasting (+0.38 SD, p < 0.001) and 2-hour OGTT glucose concentrations (+0.29 SD, p < 0.05). Linear mixed-effect model accounting for intrapair correlations and interactions confirmed that twins were thinner but fatter across the age range. Data on maternal morbidity and prematurity were not available in this cohort. African populations are known to have a muscular (less adipose) body composition. Demonstration of a thin-fat phenotype in twins in a low socio-economic African country supports the thesis that it could be a manifestation of early life undernutrition and not exclusive to Indians. This phenotype could increase risk of diabetes and related conditions.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Wagh, Rucha","Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","Bandyopadhyay, Souvik","Yajnik, Pranav","Prasad, Rashmi B.","Otiv, Suhas","Byberg, Stine","Hennild, Ditte Egegaard","Gomes, Gabriel Marciano","Christensen, Kaare","Sodemann, Morten","Jensen, Dorte Møller","Yajnik, Chittaranjan S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-617334"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Yajnik, Chittaranjan S."],"country":["Guinea-Bissau","India","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bandim Health Project","Cytel Inc.","KEM Hospital","Lund University"],"keyword":["Adiposity","Adult","Birth Weight","Body composition","Diabetes mellitus","Female","Guinea Bissau","Guinea Bissau epidemiology","Humans","Male","Malnutrition","Pregnancy","Twins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"twins in guinea bissau have a thin fat body composition compared to singletons","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2021.07.07.21260161v2.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The principal investigator (MBA) received a combined grant from Forsknings-og Innovations Styrelsen, the University of Southern Denmark, and Odense University Hospital. Den Danske Forsknings Fond, Odense University Hospital, Fonden for Lægevidenskabens Fremme and Aase and Ejnar Danielsen’s Foundation supported the data collection. CSY was a visiting professor to the University of Southern Denmark and Danish Diabetes Academy during this work, supported by Novo Nordisk Fonden. The funding sources had no role in the study design, data collection, data analysis or in writing of this manuscript."],"id":"S01-000.00-617334","identifier":[{"id":"35373734","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85128384987","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-9a203da6-934e-486d-8e40-9200fd8e48f9"],"keyword":["Adult","Birth Weight","Body Composition","Diabetes Mellitus","Female","Guinea-Bissau","Guinea-Bissau/epidemiology","Humans","Male","Malnutrition","Pregnancy","Twins","adiposity","early life undernutrition","thin-fat"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E1854F05049FB78B4632DA3BFB66BFEE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2021.07.07.21260161v2.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"kem hospital","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"KEM Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, Centre for Global Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Open - Bandim","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of SDCO - Steno Diabetes Center Odense","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Endocrinology (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"in","key":"cytel inc","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Cytel Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gw","key":"bandim health project","loc":["Guinea-Bissau","Africa"],"name":"Bandim Health Project","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rucha","key":"waghruchapau","last":"Wagh","name":"Wagh, Rucha","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"bjerregaardandersenmortenpau","last":"Bjerregaard-Andersen","locid":"a8a0b3c8-4070-4770-86b2-1cb837092b6b","name":"Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4128-5714","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Souvik","key":"bandyopadhyaysouvikpau","last":"Bandyopadhyay","name":"Bandyopadhyay, Souvik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pranav","key":"yajnikpranavpau","last":"Yajnik","name":"Yajnik, Pranav","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rashmi B.","key":"prasadrashmibpau","last":"Prasad","name":"Prasad, Rashmi B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Suhas","key":"otivsuhaspau","last":"Otiv","name":"Otiv, Suhas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"bybergstinepau","last":"Byberg","name":"Byberg, Stine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Egegaard","key":"hennildditteegegaardpau","last":"Hennild","name":"Hennild, Ditte Egegaard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Gabriel Marciano","key":"gomesgabrielmarcianopau","last":"Gomes","name":"Gomes, Gabriel Marciano","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaare","key":"christensenkaarepau","last":"Christensen","locid":"35c0eca6-0f49-465b-9bbd-ce71bcf2c4ac","name":"Christensen, Kaare","orcid":"0000-0002-5429-5292","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"sodemannmortenpau","last":"Sodemann","locid":"e4e58879-7d72-4665-880c-38ad97d0ebe5","name":"Sodemann, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-2500","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Møller","key":"jensendortemøllerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a221b393-70f9-4f53-902e-63d1a13f8f60","name":"Jensen, Dorte Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-3298-9824","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chittaranjan S.","key":"yajnikchittaranjanspau","last":"Yajnik","name":"Yajnik, Chittaranjan S.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35373734"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s2040174422000150","issn":["20401744","20401752"],"issn_org":["20401744"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Developmental Origins of Health and Disease","pages":"787-793","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Developmental Origins of Health and Disease","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128384987"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9a203da6-934e-486d-8e40-9200fd8e48f9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Twins in Guinea-Bissau have a 'thin-fat' body composition compared to singletons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-617334","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Pharmacokinetics is the cornerstone of understanding drug absorption, distribution, metabolism, and elimination. It is also the key to describing variability in drug response caused by drug-drug interactions (DDIs), pharmacogenetics, impaired kidney and liver function, etc. This tutorial aims to provide a guideline and step-by-step tutorial on essential considerations when designing clinical pharmacokinetic studies and reporting results. This includes a comprehensive guide on how to conduct the statistical analysis and a complete code for the statistical software R. As an example, we created a mock dataset simulating a clinical pharmacokinetic DDI study with 12 subjects who were administered 2 mg oral midazolam with and without an inducer of cytochrome P450 3A. We provide a step-by-step guide to the statistical analysis of this clinical pharmacokinetic study, including sample size/power calculation, descriptive statistics, noncompartmental analyses, and hypothesis testing. The different analyses and parameters are described in detail, and we provide a complete R code ready to use in supplementary files. Finally, we discuss important considerations when designing and reporting clinical pharmacokinetic studies. The scope of this tutorial is not limited to DDI studies, and with minor adjustments, it applies to all types of clinical pharmacokinetic studies. This work was done by early career researchers for early career researchers. We hope this tutorial may help early career researchers when getting started on their own pharmacokinetic studies. We encourage you to use this as an inspiration and starting point and continuously evolve your statistical skills.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Dunvald, Ann-Cathrine","Iversen, Ditte Bork","Svendsen, Andreas Ludvig Ohm","Agergaard, Katrine","Kuhlmann, Ida Berglund","Mortensen, Christina","Andersen, Nanna Elman","Järvinen, Erkka","Stage, Tore Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-626105"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Stage, Tore Bjerregaard"],"keyword":["Cytochrome P 450 CYP3A metabolism","Drug Interactions","Humans","Midazolam pharmacokinetics","Models Biological"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tutorial statistical analysis and reporting of clinical pharmacokinetic studies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cts.13305","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-626105","identifier":[{"id":"85131329173","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9372427","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35570335","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b8750b86-5de4-4a8f-82ae-241375911aba"],"keyword":["Cytochrome P-450 CYP3A Inhibitors","Cytochrome P-450 CYP3A/metabolism","Drug Interactions","Humans","Midazolam/pharmacokinetics","Models, Biological"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-642DCE5E298463915CA60A20BF33584D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cts.13305","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/203790605/Clinical_Translational_Sci_2022_Dunvald_Tutorial_Statistical_analysis_and_reporting_of_clinical_pharmacokinetic.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology, Pharmacy and Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann-Cathrine Dalgård","key":"dunvaldpau","last":"Dunvald","locid":"0cc5ad63-2aa5-48e4-94cb-655a8b0a5394","name":"Dunvald, Ann-Cathrine","name_org":"Dunvald, Ann-Cathrine Dalgård","orcid":"0000-0001-7574-0909","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Bork","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"7e67054c-25a8-4498-ba58-0b377014cfb8","name":"Iversen, Ditte Bork","orcid":"0000-0002-5519-9091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Ludvig Ohm","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"e8b52e19-61d6-4e57-b514-eb1ddd10a7bc","name":"Svendsen, Andreas Ludvig Ohm","orcid":"0000-0001-8050-6447","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine","key":"agergaardpau","last":"Agergaard","locid":"a0a9c56e-0d89-4595-ab00-a1f184678a51","name":"Agergaard, Katrine","orcid":"0000-0002-4961-4797","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Berglund","key":"kuhlmannpau","last":"Kuhlmann","locid":"4e4135f0-8ab4-4a29-a123-a8e810d17df9","name":"Kuhlmann, Ida Berglund","orcid":"0000-0003-1727-1264","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"c760b708-5cf8-4672-9652-2137a4aa0d3e","name":"Mortensen, Christina","orcid":"0000-0001-9983-9196","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Elman","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"00f385a0-a339-4dfd-87a4-c1ea54bac2bc","name":"Andersen, Nanna Elman","orcid":"0000-0001-5750-8911","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erkka","key":"järvinenpau","last":"Järvinen","locid":"7e1c52ca-c64b-4ac8-8b2c-c25effd73ad5","name":"Järvinen, Erkka","orcid":"0000-0001-8970-5194","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tore Bjerregaard","key":"stagepau","last":"Stage","locid":"b794c141-d9c5-4082-b8c5-b69f854d4c7c","name":"Stage, Tore Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-4698-4389","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35570335"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cts.13305","issn":["17528054","17528062"],"issn_org":["17528062"],"issue":"8","journal":"Clinical and Translational Science","pages":"1856-1866","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Clinical and Translational Science","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131329173"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b8750b86-5de4-4a8f-82ae-241375911aba"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Tutorial: Statistical analysis and reporting of clinical pharmacokinetic studies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-626105","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Azole antimycotics and nystatin oral solution are used to treat oral candidiasis. Azoles inhibit cytochrome (CYP) P450-dependent metabolism of warfarin, which could increase the anticoagulant effect of warfarin. Nystatin is not expected to interfere with warfarin metabolism, but current data are conflicting. With this study, we aimed to explore the potential drug-drug interactions between warfarin and azole anti-mycotics used in the treatment of oral candidiasis, that is, systemic fluconazole, miconazole oral gel, and nystatin oral solution. METHODS: By linking clinical data on international normalized ratio (INR) measurements with administra-tive data on filled prescriptions of warfarin and antimycotics during 2000-2015, we explored INR changes in warfarin users relative to initiation of systemic fluconazole (n = 413), miconazole oral gel (n = 330), and nystatin oral solution (n = 399). RESULTS: We found a significant increase in mean INR of 0.83 (95% confidence interval [CI] 0.61-1.04) and 1.27 (95% CI 0.94-1.59) following initiation of systemic fluconazole and miconazole oral gel, respec-tively. Also, the proportion of patients experiencing an INR-value above 5 was increased after initiation of fluconazole (from 4.3% to 15.3%) and miconazole (from 5.5% to 30.1%). INR was unaffected by initiation of nystatin oral solution (mean change 0.08; 95% CI-0.10 to 0.25). CONCLUSION: Initiation of systemic fluconazole and miconazole oral gel was associated with increased INR in warfarin users. A similar association was not found for nystatin oral solution, which thus appears to be the safest alternative when treating oral candidiasis in warfarin users. (C) 2020 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Iversen, Ditte B.","Hellfritzsch, Maja","Stage, Tore B.","Aabenhus, Rune M.","Lind, Bent S.","Pottegård, Anton"],"cuid":["S03-097.81-022881"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Iversen, Ditte B.","Iversen, Ditte Bork"],"keyword":["Antimycotics","Drug Interactions","Warfarin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antimycotic treatment of oral candidiasis in warfarin users","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332615959/Antimycotic_Treatment_of_Oral_Candidiasis_in_2_11.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Martin Thomsen Ernst (University of Southern Denmark) is acknowledged for help with data management. Funding: None."],"id":"S03-097.81-022881","identifier":[{"id":"85097779702","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000647677500005","type":"wos"},{"id":"33176127","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8c0a06f2-967c-4ba5-9d61-1c7eea139ea5","ku-ccfea6f0-44a2-4b3d-a71a-86be9c3f3cff","sdu-ea62f3f5-449d-4ff1-8cb2-f2355c24e3ca"],"keyword":["Antimycotics","Drug interactions","Warfarin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-941412A3DBD4E86563ADA9BA65720DC4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332615959/Antimycotic_Treatment_of_Oral_Candidiasis_in_2_11.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178946034/Manuscript_track_changes_OFF.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universitie