-0f1bf0f6-8ecc-4987-bdd2-13e1bb9a7b51"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Gastroenterologiske symptomer hos patienter med diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.57-009601","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Sub-Saharan Africa has the highest natural twinning rate in the world. Unfortunately, due to lack of adequate care during pregnancy, labor and postnatally, twin mortality in Sub-Saharan Africa also remains very high. Thus, it has been estimated that one in five twins dies during the childhood years. In spite of this, surprisingly few twin studies have been conducted in the region, making additional epidemiological data much needed. In 2009, we established one of the first twin registries in Sub-Saharan Africa at the Bandim Health Project in Guinea-Bissau. The registry had two main objectives. First, we wanted to describe the twinning rate and mortality patterns among newborn twins, including mortality risk factors and hospitalization patterns. Such studies can help the local clinicians improve twin health by identifying the most vulnerable children. Second, and in light of the rapidly increasing diabetes rates in Africa, we wanted to use the registry to particularly focus on metabolic disorders. Twins are often born with low birth weight, which according to the 'thrifty phenotype hypothesis' could predispose them to metabolic disorders later in life. Yet, no such 'fetal programming' data have previously been available from African twins despite the fact that nutritional patterns and influences from other factors (e.g., infections) could be markedly different here compared to high-income settings. In this article, we summarize the findings and current status of the Guinea-Bissau twin registry.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","Gomes, Gabriel Marciano","Egegaard Hennild, Ditte","Jensen, Dorte Møller","Christensen, Kaare","Sodemann, Morten","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Aaby, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586566"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"corpau":["Endokronoligi - Bariatri og Diabetes"],"corresponding_author":["Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten"],"country":["Guinea-Bissau"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bandim Health Project"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the guinea bissau twin registry update a platform for studying twin mortality and metabolic disease","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/152550424/The_Guinea_Bissau_Twin_Registry_Update.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586566","identifier":[{"id":"85069483986","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31317858","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-2eabc500-6cfd-4be0-be4e-5c0915839ba5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-41B95E73A1FC627F801783A25EE552B1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/152550424/The_Guinea_Bissau_Twin_Registry_Update.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, Centre for Global Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Endocrinology (Esbjerg)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gw","key":"bandim health project","loc":["Guinea-Bissau","Africa"],"name":"Bandim Health Project","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"endokronoligi bariatri og diabetes","name":"Endokronoligi - Bariatri og Diabetes","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"bjerregaardandersenpau","last":"Bjerregaard-Andersen","locid":"a8a0b3c8-4070-4770-86b2-1cb837092b6b","name":"Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4128-5714","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gabriel Marciano","key":"gomespau","last":"Gomes","name":"Gomes, Gabriel Marciano","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Egegaard","key":"hennildpau","last":"Hennild","locid":"50d9cee4-514a-4c76-a3cf-36ec496a853f","name":"Egegaard Hennild, Ditte","name_org":"Hennild, Ditte Egegaard","orcid":"0000-0001-6769-0913","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a221b393-70f9-4f53-902e-63d1a13f8f60","name":"Jensen, Dorte Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-3298-9824","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaare","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"35c0eca6-0f49-465b-9bbd-ce71bcf2c4ac","name":"Christensen, Kaare","orcid":"0000-0002-5429-5292","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"sodemannpau","last":"Sodemann","locid":"e4e58879-7d72-4665-880c-38ad97d0ebe5","name":"Sodemann, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-2500","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"becknielsenpau","last":"Beck-Nielsen","locid":"0e78b588-9e9c-4acc-a1b8-8bcccea0b5a5","name":"Beck-Nielsen, Henning","orcid":"0000-0002-7428-7898","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"aabypau","last":"Aaby","name":"Aaby, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31317858"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/thg.2019.39","issn":["18324274","18392628"],"issn_org":["18324274"],"issue":"6","journal":"Twin Research and Human Genetics","pages":"554-560","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Twin Research and Human Genetics","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069483986"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2eabc500-6cfd-4be0-be4e-5c0915839ba5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Guinea-Bissau Twin Registry Update : A Platform for Studying Twin Mortality and Metabolic Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-586566","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Twins may be at increased risk of dysglycaemic disorders due to adverse fetal conditions. Data from Africa regarding this association is limited. We studied impaired glucose tolerance (IGT) and other types of dysglycemia among twins and singletons in Guinea-Bissau. METHODS: The study was conducted from February 2011 until March 2012 at the Bandim Health Project, a health and demographic surveillance system site in the capital Bissau. Twins (n = 209) and singletons (n = 182) were recruited from a previously established cohort. Oral glucose tolerance tests (OGTT) were performed, along with anthropometrics and collection of clinical and dietary data. RESULTS: Median age was 16.6 and 14.2 years between twins and singletons, respectively (P = 0.08). Mean birth weight was 2410 vs. 3090 g, respectively (P < 0.001). Twins had higher median fasting- and two hour capillary plasma glucose, 5.4(3.2-8.2) vs. 5.0(3.2-11.5) mmol/L (P < 0.001) and 6.8(3.4-11.3) vs. 6.2(3.2-12.1) mmol/L (P < 0.001), respectively, compared to singletons. The prevalence of IGT was 2.5 % (5/209) vs. 3.5 % (6/182) (RR = 0.73, 95 % CI: 0.20-2.64). 12 % (25/209) of twins had impaired fasting glucose (IFG), compared to 3.5 % (6/182) of singletons (3.63, 1.53-8.62). Dysglycemia (IGT and/or IFG or overt diabetes) was found in 17 % (35/209) vs. 9 % (16/182) (1.90, 1.08-3.37), respectively. CONCLUSIONS: Twins had higher glucose levels in both the fasting and postprandial state. This may indicate a detrimental effect of the twin fetal environment on glucose metabolism later in life, a result contrary to Scandinavian register studies. The IGT burden was low in this young age group and the risk was similar in twins and singletons.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Egegaard Hennild, Ditte","Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","Joaquím, Luis Carlos","Christensen, Kaare","Sodemann, Morten","Beck-Nielsen, Henning","Jensen, Dorte Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-644273"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Guinea-Bissau"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guinean Diabetes Association","INDEPTH Network"],"keyword":["Diabetes","Impaired fasting glucose","Impaired glucose tolerance","Low birth weight","Sub Saharan Africa","Twins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence of impaired glucose tolerance and other types of dysglycaemia among young twins and singletons in guinea bissau","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12902-016-0126-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-644273","identifier":[{"id":"84982737872","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4973540","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27491662","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-f8496b2c-7908-4038-b443-549400e0b705"],"keyword":["Diabetes","Fetal origins hypothesis","Impaired fasting glucose","Impaired glucose tolerance","Low birth weight","Sub-Saharan Africa","Twins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-14565DD3E93E7529EBB577C99DF1A398"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12902-016-0126-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121343387/Prevalence_of_impaired_glucose_tolerance_and_other_types_of_dysglycaemia_among_young_twins_and_singletons_in_Guinea_Bissau.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gw","key":"indepth network","loc":["Guinea-Bissau","Africa"],"name":"INDEPTH Network","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gw","key":"guinean diabetes association","loc":["Guinea-Bissau","Africa"],"name":"Guinean Diabetes Association","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte","key":"egegaardhennildpau","last":"Egegaard Hennild","locid":"50d9cee4-514a-4c76-a3cf-36ec496a853f","name":"Egegaard Hennild, Ditte","orcid":"0000-0001-6769-0913","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"bjerregaardandersenpau","last":"Bjerregaard-Andersen","locid":"a8a0b3c8-4070-4770-86b2-1cb837092b6b","name":"Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4128-5714","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis Carlos","key":"joaquímpau","last":"Joaquím","name":"Joaquím, Luis Carlos","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaare","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"35c0eca6-0f49-465b-9bbd-ce71bcf2c4ac","name":"Christensen, Kaare","orcid":"0000-0002-5429-5292","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"sodemannpau","last":"Sodemann","locid":"e4e58879-7d72-4665-880c-38ad97d0ebe5","name":"Sodemann, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-2500","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"becknielsenpau","last":"Beck-Nielsen","locid":"0e78b588-9e9c-4acc-a1b8-8bcccea0b5a5","name":"Beck-Nielsen, Henning","orcid":"0000-0002-7428-7898","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a221b393-70f9-4f53-902e-63d1a13f8f60","name":"Jensen, Dorte Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-3298-9824","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27491662"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12902-016-0126-6","issn":["14726823"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Endocrine Disorders","paperid":"46","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Endocrine Disorders","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84982737872"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f8496b2c-7908-4038-b443-549400e0b705"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Prevalence of impaired glucose tolerance and other types of dysglycaemia among young twins and singletons in Guinea-Bissau","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-644273","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The prevalence of diabetes mellitus (DM) is expected to increase in sub-Saharan Africa. Patients with HIV are at particular risk. We investigated the DM burden among antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve patients with HIV in Guinea-Bissau. METHODS: Patients were consecutively included. Demographic and lifestyle data were collected and one fasting blood glucose (FBG) measurement was used to diagnose DM (FBG≥7.0 mmol/L) and impaired fasting glucose (IFG) (FBG≥6.1 and <7.0 mmol/L). RESULTS: By June 2015, 953 newly diagnosed ART-naïve patients with HIV had been included in the study of whom 893 (93.7%) were fasting at the time of inclusion. Median age among the fasting patients was 37 years (IQR 30-46 years) and 562 (62.9%) were women. The prevalence of DM was 5.8% (52/893) while 5.6% (50/893) had IFG. DM was associated with family history of DM (OR 3.92, 95% CI 1.78 to 8.63), being 41-50 years (OR 2.98, 95% CI 1.18 to 7.49) or older than 50 years (OR 3.14, 95% CI 1.09 to 9.07) and Fula ethnicity (OR 2.72, 95% CI 1.12 to 6.62). CONCLUSIONS: DM prevalence was higher among younger patients compared with the background population in Bissau. Traditional risk factors for DM such as advancing age and a family history of DM apply also for ART-naïve patients with HIV.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Steiniche, Ditte","Jespersen, Sanne","Erikstrup, Christian","Krarup, Henrik","Handberg, Aase","Østergaard, Lars","Haraldsdottir, Thorny","Medina, Candida","Gomes Correira, Faustino","Laursen, Alex Lund","Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","Wejse, Christian","Hønge, Bo Langhoff"],"cuid":["S03-099.50-000042"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Africa"],"corpau":["Bissau HIV Cohort study group"],"country":["Guinea-Bissau"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INDEPTH Network","Ministry of Health, Guinea-Bissau"],"keyword":["Adult","Age Factors","Anti HIV Agents","B